  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"For the period ended October 31, 2026, Corvane Analytics is in breach of its Revenue to Plan covenant, with revenue at {{fact:e959bfd5-abb7-47e5-a334-99dfbb8654e2}} of plan against a required {{fact:3755719f-7547-4045-a3fd-6739b19e4094}}. The borrower's compliance certificate reports the same figure and does not claim compliance. The Minimum Runway and Minimum Unrestricted Cash covenants are met, although the bank's monitoring shows cash headroom declining each month since August. The breach work item has been decided and escalated to committee, where the bank's response will be determined.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"Minimum Runway was met. The bank calculated {{fact:c0543b5b-acf2-4bda-bfcd-364d3f12b83f}} against a requirement of {{fact:dfaf42df-7646-4827-a9a7-f8991d06bf9a}}, a cushion of {{fact:f84a80af-77a6-4bb1-b899-93c468ca133f}}. The certificate reports {{fact:d0627a88-f2ac-4ae5-80ab-96e40d1af32b}}. Minimum Unrestricted Cash was met at {{fact:f6e501ae-5be2-4942-95b6-ecc0bf3ee257}} against {{fact:cf41bfe4-6836-4f51-aabf-2439f8c303cc}}, a cushion of {{fact:808ba721-2a2c-424f-987c-32d347db04d9}}, and the certificate reports {{fact:4abfc950-eae4-43f4-9c95-6e2d0224cc29}}. Revenue to Plan is in breach at {{fact:e959bfd5-abb7-47e5-a334-99dfbb8654e2}} against a floor of {{fact:3755719f-7547-4045-a3fd-6739b19e4094}}, a negative cushion of {{fact:1fe991a3-04a0-442a-b354-f9570c0a7fb5}}. The certificate reports {{fact:8204fb36-f1b7-4530-8172-d344c070b721}} and acknowledges non-compliance, so the borrower's figures agree with the bank's calculation on each covenant.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The most significant item is the high-severity Revenue to Plan breach, which has been decided and escalated to committee. The medium-severity signals relate to the same shortfall. Revenue was below plan, and the covenant measure sits below its threshold rather than merely near it. A low-severity signal shows revenue covenant headroom deteriorating each month since August. That headroom turned negative in September and widened to {{fact:1fe991a3-04a0-442a-b354-f9570c0a7fb5}} in October, which points to a worsening trend rather than a single-month miss. Another low-severity signal shows unrestricted cash headroom declining each month to {{fact:808ba721-2a2c-424f-987c-32d347db04d9}} in October. Reviewers may wish to examine whether continued burn alongside the revenue shortfall explains this decline.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
 ],
